<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Flow xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT MUST STAY INSIDE THE ROOT <Flow> ELEMENT. A comment placed ABOVE <Flow>
        breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading "unable to find matching parent
        xml file" error.

        =====================================================================================
        🔴 AMENDED 2026-08-20 (Tranche 2, Workstream A3). THE PARAGRAPH BELOW IS RETAINED, NOT
        DELETED, BECAUSE THE HAZARD IT NAMES IS STILL LIVE. BUT ITS FIRST SENTENCE IS NO LONGER
        LITERALLY TRUE AND IS RETRACTED HERE, AT THE TOP, SO IT CANNOT BE READ STANDALONE.
        =====================================================================================
        WHAT CHANGED. Is_Signed's default branch is now CONNECTED, to a new decision named
        Is_Declined. That decision routes ONE value, Status__c = 'Declined', to the previously
        orphaned Set_Signed_False assignment. Every other status, including acquisition's
        terminal 'Sent', falls through Is_Declined's OWN default branch, which has no connector
        and therefore reaches an end. Set_Signed_False itself is unchanged; it simply stops
        being unreachable.

        🔴 WHAT DID NOT CHANGE, AND WHAT IS STILL FORBIDDEN. The hazard the paragraph below
        describes is a BLANKET `Status != 'Signed' => false` rule. That is still forbidden and
        would still break acquisition exactly as described. Connecting Is_Signed's default
        DIRECTLY to Set_Signed_False, which is the specific edit the paragraph warns against,
        is still the wrong edit and is still an outage. The safe form is the one now built: a
        VALUE NAMED intermediate decision. Read the whole paragraph, then read this block again.

        =====================================================================================
        RETAINED FROM 2026-08-16 (acquisition NDA sequence reversal). ⚠ ITS OPENING CLAIM, THAT
        THE FALSE BRANCH IS UNCONNECTED, WAS TRUE FROM 2026-08-16 TO 2026-08-20 AND IS NOW
        SUPERSEDED BY THE BLOCK ABOVE. THE REST STILL APPLIES VERBATIM.
        =====================================================================================
        THE Is_Signed DECISION'S FALSE BRANCH IS DEFINED BUT UNCONNECTED, AND THIS IS LOAD-BEARING
        - DO NOT "FINISH" IT. The
        Set_Signed_False assignment exists in this flow's metadata, but Is_Signed carries a
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Not Signed</defaultConnectorLabel> with NO <defaultConnector>, so
        nothing ever routes to Set_Signed_False. The flow therefore only ever SETS the checkbox
        true; it never clears it. This is despite the description above (prior to this comment)
        having claimed the derivation runs "in both directions" - it does not, and the second half
        was never implemented. That claim has been corrected in the description, but a flow editor
        who trusts the OLD wording, sees an unconnected assignment sitting right there, and
        connects it as an "unfinished job" will silently break acquisition NDA processing.

        WHY: the acquisition NDA sequence is now Pending -> Received -> Signed -> Sent, with
        'Sent' as the TERMINAL step (not 'Signed' - see objects/NDA__c/recordTypes/
        Acquisition_NDA.recordType-meta.xml and RecordStageAdvanceService.NDA_ACQUISITION_NEXT_STAGE
        for the full rationale). The Opportunity gate NDA_Signed_Before_Deal_Progression blocks
        Underwriting / LOI / Under Contract (PSA) / About to Close / Closed Won unless
        Primary_NDA__r.NDA_Signed__c is true. The reorder is safe TODAY only because the checkbox
        LATCHES: an acquisition NDA moving from 'Signed' to 'Sent' keeps NDA_Signed__c = TRUE,
        because nothing ever sets it back to false.

        IF ANYONE CONNECTS THE DEFAULT BRANCH TO Set_Signed_False, the final Advance Stage click
        (Signed -> Sent) will set NDA_Signed__c back to FALSE and LOCK the deal out of every stage
        past the NDA gate - the button will appear to complete the NDA and will in fact un-sign it.
        A disposition NDA has no equivalent hazard (its own 'Sent' is NOT terminal - see
        RecordStageAdvanceService.NDA_DISPOSITION_NEXT_STAGE), so if the two-directional behaviour
        is ever genuinely needed, whoever implements it MUST exempt the acquisition terminal
        'Sent' explicitly (e.g. branch on RecordType.DeveloperName, or on Status__c != 'Sent' for
        Acquisition_NDA rows) rather than restoring a blanket Status != 'Signed' => false rule.

        =====================================================================================
        🔴 WHY THE 2026-08-20 IMPLEMENTATION DOES NOT USE RecordType.DeveloperName, WHICH IS
        WHAT THE PARAGRAPH DIRECTLY ABOVE SUGGESTED. THE NARROWER FORM IS ALSO THE SAFER ONE.
        =====================================================================================
        The requirement is to clear the checkbox on DECLINED ONLY, which is strictly narrower
        than "everything that is not Signed" and needs no record type test at all:

        'Declined' IS EXPOSED ONLY ON THE Disposition_NDA RECORD TYPE. NDA__c.Status__c's own
        description states the split in terms: Acquisition_NDA exposes Pending, Sent, Received,
        Signed; Disposition_NDA exposes Not Sent, Sent, Signed, Declined. An acquisition NDA can
        therefore never carry the value the new branch tests for, so acquisition's terminal
        'Sent' is STRUCTURALLY UNREACHABLE from Set_Signed_False. The exemption is achieved by
        NAMING A VALUE rather than by TESTING A RECORD TYPE.

        THAT IS MORE ROBUST THAN THE SUGGESTION ABOVE, FOR TWO REASONS THIS REPO HAS MEASURED:
          1. A record type test breaks on rows still sitting on the MASTER record type.
             RecordStageAdvanceService still carries a null/Master fallback, and
             TestDataFactory deliberately degrades to NO record type when one is absent from or
             unavailable in a scratch org. A Master row is a normal fixture shape here, and a
             RecordType.DeveloperName = 'Disposition_NDA' branch would silently skip it.
          2. A record type test breaks on a record type RENAME; a value named test does not.
             NdaSelector.queryExpiryAlerts records the related failure mode, where a record type
             filter shipped a feature inert.

        ⚠ THE ONE THING THIS FORM DEPENDS ON, STATED SO IT IS NOT REDISCOVERED THE HARD WAY:
        it relies on 'Declined' STAYING off the Acquisition_NDA record type. If 'Declined' is
        ever added to Acquisition_NDA, this flow starts clearing NDA_Signed__c on acquisition
        NDAs and the Opportunity gate NDA_Signed_Before_Deal_Progression locks those deals out.
        Anyone editing objects/NDA__c/recordTypes/Acquisition_NDA.recordType-meta.xml must read
        this block first. That is a cheaper and more visible dependency than the Master row
        problem a record type test would have carried permanently.

        BEHAVIOUR CHANGE, STATED PLAINLY: a disposition NDA moving Signed -> Declined now clears
        NDA_Signed__c, where previously it stayed true. Date_Signed__c is STILL never cleared, by
        design, so a declined party retains a signature date alongside a false checkbox. Any
        consumer deciding "is this party signed" must gate on Status__c, NOT on Date_Signed__c
        and NOT on NDA_Signed__c alone.
    -->
    <apiVersion>67.0</apiVersion>
    <assignments>
        <name>Set_Signed_False</name>
        <label>Set Signed False</label>
        <locationX>302</locationX>
        <locationY>288</locationY>
        <assignmentItems>
            <assignToReference>$Record.NDA_Signed__c</assignToReference>
            <operator>Assign</operator>
            <value>
                <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
            </value>
        </assignmentItems>
    </assignments>
    <assignments>
        <name>Set_Signed_True</name>
        <label>Set Signed True</label>
        <locationX>50</locationX>
        <locationY>288</locationY>
        <assignmentItems>
            <assignToReference>$Record.NDA_Signed__c</assignToReference>
            <operator>Assign</operator>
            <value>
                <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
            </value>
        </assignmentItems>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Needs_Signed_Date</targetReference>
        </connector>
    </assignments>
    <assignments>
        <name>Stamp_Signed_Date</name>
        <label>Stamp Signed Date</label>
        <locationX>50</locationX>
        <locationY>504</locationY>
        <assignmentItems>
            <assignToReference>$Record.Date_Signed__c</assignToReference>
            <operator>Assign</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Flow.CurrentDate</elementReference>
            </value>
        </assignmentItems>
    </assignments>
    <decisions>
        <name>Is_Declined</name>
        <label>Is Declined?</label>
        <locationX>302</locationX>
        <locationY>180</locationY>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Not Declined</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Status_Is_Declined</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.Status__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>Declined</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Set_Signed_False</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Declined</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <name>Is_Signed</name>
        <label>Is Signed?</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>180</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Is_Declined</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Not Signed</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Status_Is_Signed</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.Status__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>Signed</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Set_Signed_True</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Signed</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <name>Needs_Signed_Date</name>
        <label>Needs Signed Date?</label>
        <locationX>50</locationX>
        <locationY>396</locationY>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Already set</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Date_Signed_Is_Blank</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.Date_Signed__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Stamp_Signed_Date</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Stamp</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>Derives NDA_Signed__c from Status__c on every save. &apos;Signed&apos; sets the checkbox TRUE. From 2026-08-20, &apos;Declined&apos; sets it FALSE via the new Is_Declined decision on Is_Signed&apos;s default branch. NO other status touches it, so it still latches true through Sent, Received, Pending and Not Sent. &apos;Declined&apos; is exposed ONLY on Disposition_NDA, so acquisition&apos;s TERMINAL &apos;Sent&apos; can never reach the clearing branch and NDA_Signed_Before_Deal_Progression is unaffected; that value-named exemption is used deliberately instead of a RecordType.DeveloperName test, which would break on Master-record-type rows. Also stamps Date_Signed__c to TODAY the first time Status reaches &apos;Signed&apos; with a blank date. It NEVER clears Date_Signed__c, so a declined party keeps a signature date beside a false checkbox: gate on Status__c, not on either field alone. Before-save, so rules reading NDA_Signed__c see the synced value in the same transaction. Read the in-root XML comment before editing any branch.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <interviewLabel>NDA Signed Status Sync {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>NDA Signed Status Sync</label>
    <processType>AutoLaunchedFlow</processType>
    <start>
        <locationX>50</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Is_Signed</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <object>NDA__c</object>
        <recordTriggerType>CreateAndUpdate</recordTriggerType>
        <triggerType>RecordBeforeSave</triggerType>
    </start>
    <status>Active</status>
</Flow>
